{"id": "trm:omkara", "term": "oṃkāra", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: the syllable Oṃ (akṣara), which is all this and all time, and is the self; it has three measures a, u, m, and a fourth that is without measure.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:1", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:8", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:12"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}}
{"id": "trm:aksara", "term": "akṣara", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: the syllable (Oṃ); \"etad akṣaram\" — this syllable — is all this.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:1"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "literal": "syllable; imperishable"}
{"id": "trm:catuspad", "term": "catuṣpād", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: \"four-quartered\", said of the self (ātman): its four quarters are vaiśvānara, taijasa, prājña and the fourth.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:2"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "literal": "four-footed"}
{"id": "trm:vaisvanara", "term": "vaiśvānara", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: the first quarter of the self; its station is waking, it is outward-knowing, seven-limbed and nineteen-mouthed, an enjoyer of the gross; it is the measure a.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:3", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:9"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}}
{"id": "trm:taijasa", "term": "taijasa", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: the second quarter of the self; its station is dream, it is inward-knowing, an enjoyer of the \"separated\"/subtle; it is the measure u.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:4", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:10"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "literal": "the brilliant one"}
{"id": "trm:prajna-mandukya", "term": "prājña (Māṇḍūkya)", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: the third quarter of the self; its station is deep sleep; it is become one, a mass of cognition, made of bliss, an enjoyer of bliss, with thought as its mouth; it is lord of all, knower of all, inner controller and source of all; it is the measure m.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:5", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:6", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:11"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}}
{"id": "trm:turiya", "term": "turīya", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text the fourth (caturtha) quarter of the self, not knowing inward or outward, unseen, not to be dealt with, the stilling of the world, auspicious, non-dual; without measure; it is the self and is to be known.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:7", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:12"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}, "literal": "the fourth"}
{"id": "trm:jagrat", "term": "jāgarita", "language": "Sanskrit", "definitions": [{"lineage": "lin:upanisadic", "definition": "In this text: waking, the station (sthāna) of vaiśvānara.", "sources": ["src:mandukya-upanisad"], "rests_on": ["tea:mandukya-upanisad:3", "tea:mandukya-upanisad:9"]}], "related": [], "concepts": [], "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [], "protocol": "insight-p1-single+spot"}}
